    "body": "## Summary\n\n- add a first-party Cloudflare Worker + D1 receiver for the authorized private-friends telemetry schema\n- add strict envelope/event validation, exact-origin CORS, request and event-volume limits, durable batch deduplication, 30-day retention, and owner-only summary/session/export endpoints\n- add resilient client batching/retry/offline transport with a separate immutable deployment config\n- keep transport disabled and endpoint empty until the external Cloudflare account, D1 database, token, and GitHub deployment settings are provisioned\n- preserve the existing player UI: no consent, refusal, cookie, analytics, or settings UI is added\n- keep source and GitHub Pages mirrors byte-identical\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 tools/test_behavioral_telemetry.py`\n- `node tools/test_behavioral_telemetry_runtime.mjs`\n- `ALLOW_NETWORK_SMOKE=1 npm --prefix telemetry-receiver run check` (7/7)\n- Wrangler 4.122.0 dry-run with Node 24\n- source/docs byte parity\n- changed-scope diff and YAML validation\n- focused Stage 7 runtime smokes pass, including toast geometry/click-only behavior\n\n## Known baseline drift\n\nTwo legacy Stage 7 source assertions remain red without touching their owned files:\n- `tools/test_stage7_first_causal_vertical_slice.py` expects the removed CTA `Продолжить`\n- `tools/test_stage7_12_first_real_battle_aftermath.py` expects the removed copy `Игра уже открыта`\n\nThese are pre-existing contract drift, not receiver regressions.\n\n## Deployment boundary\n\nMerging this PR publishes the disabled transport code to Pages safely. Production receiver deployment and client activation require external Cloudflare provisioning plus repository environment/secrets; those resources are not currently present.",
